  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_en/",
      "html": "<p>Males of Macrobrachium brasiliense become around 8.5 cm, females around 5 cm long (body length only). The species prefers soft and slightly acidic water, but thrives also well in medium hard water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_en/",
      "html": "<p>The species has a wide distribution in South America. The animals described here were imported from Peru.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_en/",
      "html": "<p>It prefers soft and slightly acidic water, but thrives also well in medium hard water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_en/",
      "html": "<p>The very attractive species changes coloration a lot depending on mood and equipment; it can be anything from whitish to deep reddish brown. It is at least the first choice for biotope aquaria with fishes from South America.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_en/",
      "html": "<p>Most freshwater shrimps from South America are difficult to raise in aquaria because their larvae develop in marine environments. Macrobrachium brasiliense is one of the very few South American species of Macrobrachium with large eggs that can be bred quite easily in home aquaria.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/macrobrachium_brasiliense_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Macrobrachium: ancient Greek, means \"with big arm\". brasiliense: means \"coming from Brazil\".</p>"
    }
  ],
